/* book Worked example: Q: A helical pair has mn = 3 mm, z1 = 20, z2 = 80, ψ = 15°, φn = 20° and b = 45 mm, and transmits 11 kW at 1450 rpm of the pinion. Find mt, d1, v, the three force components on the pinion, zv1 and the overlap ratio.
   1. Transverse module: mt = 3/cos 15° = 3/0.96593 = 3.106 mm. Pitch diameters: d1 = 3.106 × 20 = 62.12 mm, d2 = 248.47 mm; a = 155.29 mm.
   2. Pitch line velocity: v = π × 0.06212 × 1450/60 = 4.716 m/s.
   3. Tangential force: Ft = 11 000/4.716 = 2332 N.
   4. Axial thrust: Fa = 2332 × tan 15° = 2332 × 0.26795 = 625 N.
   5. Radial force: Fr = 2332 × tan 20°/cos 15° = 2332 × 0.36397/0.96593 = 879 N.
   6. Virtual teeth: zv1 = 20/cos³15° = 20/0.90122 = 22.19.
   7. Overlap ratio: 45 × sin 15°/(π × 3) = 45 × 0.25882/9.4248 = 1.24.
   Answer: mt = 3.106 mm, d1 = 62.12 mm, v = 4.716 m/s, Ft = 2332 N, Fa = 625 N, Fr = 879 N, zv1 = 22.19, overlap ratio 1.24. */
