/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The two pitch cones roll on each other without slip and share one apex.
   - Sizes are given at the large end.
   - The back cone is the cone at the large end whose surface is at right angles to the pitch cone.
   - The tooth force acts near the middle of the face.
   - Sb is in N; σb in N/mm²; b, m and R in mm; Y for zv.
   - Buckingham's dynamic load is the spur gear formula, Fd = 21v(Ceb + Ft)/(21v + √(Ceb + Ft)), and Feff = Cs Ft + Fd.
   - Sw = 0.75 b Q′ d1 K / cos γ1 with Q′ = 2zv2/(zv1 + zv2), d1 the large-end pinion diameter in mm and K = 0.16(BHN/100)² for steel.
   - Straight bevel teeth also push the shafts apart and along their axes.
   - Spiral bevel and hypoid gears (curved teeth, offset axes) follow their own standards.
*/
