/* book Worked example: Q: A 90° straight bevel pair has z1 = 20, z2 = 40, module 4 mm at the large end and face width 25 mm. Find d1, d2, γ1, γ2, R, the mean pinion radius, the mean module and both virtual tooth numbers.
   1. Pitch diameters: d1 = 4 × 20 = 80 mm, d2 = 4 × 40 = 160 mm.
   2. Pitch angles: tan γ1 = 20/40 = 0.5, so γ1 = 26.565°, γ2 = 63.435°.
   3. Cone distance: R = √(40² + 80²) = √8000 = 89.44 mm. R/3 = 29.81 mm, so b = 25 mm is allowed.
   4. Mean radius: rm1 = 40 − 25 × sin 26.565°/2 = 40 − 25 × 0.44721/2 = 40 − 5.59 = 34.41 mm.
   5. Mean module: mm = m(R − b/2)/R = 4 × 76.94/89.44 = 3.441 mm (check: 2rm1/z1 = 68.82/20 = 3.441 mm).
   6. Virtual teeth: zv1 = 20/cos 26.565° = 20/0.89443 = 22.36; zv2 = 40/cos 63.435° = 40/0.44721 = 89.44.
   Answer: d1 = 80 mm, d2 = 160 mm, γ1 = 26.57°, γ2 = 63.43°, R = 89.44 mm, rm1 = 34.41 mm, mm = 3.441 mm, zv1 = 22.36, zv2 = 89.44. */
