/* book Worked example 2: Q: The pair of the first example transmits 3 kW at 1000 rpm of the pinion. Both gears are steel, σb = 200 N/mm², 350 BHN; Cs = 1.25, e = 0.010 mm, C = 11 400 N/mm², φ = 20°. Find the factors of safety in bending and wear, and the pinion's axial and radial forces.
   1. Torque: T = 3000 × 60/(2π × 1000) = 28.65 N·m = 28 648 N·mm. Ft = 28 648/34.41 = 832.5 N.
   2. Large-end velocity: v = π × 0.080 × 1000/60 = 4.189 m/s.
   3. Beam strength of the pinion (weaker, zv1 = 22.36): Y = 0.484 − 2.87/22.36 = 0.3556; 1 − b/R = 1 − 25/89.44 = 0.7205; Sb = 200 × 25 × 4 × 0.3556 × 0.7205 = 5125 N.
   4. Buckingham: Ceb = 11 400 × 0.010 × 25 = 2850 N; Ceb + Ft = 3682.5 N; √3682.5 = 60.68; 21v = 87.96. Fd = 87.96 × 3682.5/(87.96 + 60.68) = 2179 N.
   5. Feff = 1.25 × 832.5 + 2179 = 3220 N. Bending: 5125/3220 = 1.59.
   6. Wear: Q′ = 2 × 89.44/(22.36 + 89.44) = 1.6; K = 0.16 × 3.5² = 1.96 N/mm²; Sw = 0.75 × 25 × 1.6 × 80 × 1.96/0.89443 = 5259 N. Wear: 5259/3220 = 1.63.
   7. Pinion forces: Fa1 = 832.5 × tan 20° × sin 26.565° = 832.5 × 0.36397 × 0.44721 = 135.5 N; Fr1 = 832.5 × 0.36397 × 0.89443 = 271.0 N. On the gear: axial 271.0 N, radial 135.5 N.
   Answer: Factor of safety 1.59 in bending and 1.63 in wear, both above 1.5; pinion thrust 135.5 N and radial force 271.0 N. */
