/* book Worked example: Q: A single-start worm (z1 = 1) with module 5 mm and q = 10 drives a 40-tooth wheel; the worm turns at 1440 rpm. Find d1, d2, a, the lead, the lead angle, v1 and the rubbing velocity.
   1. d1 = qm = 10 × 5 = 50 mm; d2 = m z2 = 5 × 40 = 200 mm; a = (50 + 200)/2 = 125 mm.
   2. Lead: L = z1πm = 1 × π × 5 = 15.708 mm.
   3. Lead angle: tan λ = z1/q = 1/10 = 0.1, so λ = 5.711°.
   4. Worm pitch line velocity: v1 = π × 0.050 × 1440/60 = 3.770 m/s.
   5. Rubbing velocity: vs = 3.770/cos 5.711° = 3.770/0.99504 = 3.789 m/s. Ratio i = 40 and wheel speed 1440/40 = 36 rpm.
   Answer: d1 = 50 mm, d2 = 200 mm, a = 125 mm, L = 15.71 mm, λ = 5.71°, v1 = 3.77 m/s, vs = 3.79 m/s. */
